      "content": "Concurrent saves to different observation keys can read the same global revision. After one commits, the other's `marketDataUnchanged` check fails, and this branch returns a key `Conflict` even though that key still matches the accepted command binding. Persistence does not retry failed checks. Retry global-counter-only conflicts against a fresh snapshot (while retaining the original expected key revision), or increment the counter transactionally, so unrelated saves can both succeed without weakening stale-key protection.",
